Input: {"decision_time_ms": 1790499599999, "macro_contexts": {"D1": {"context": {"always_in": "long", "always_in_relevance": "medium", "breakout_mode": true, "confidence": "medium", "decision_time_ms": 1790467199999, "directional_pressure": "bull", "evidence_against": ["The trend's middle is a 20-bar overlapping range (2357.18-2557.46, 1787356800000-1788998399999), so much of the post-spike structure is two-sided rather than a tight channel.", "1789084800000 spikes to 2680 but closes 2514.72, 165.28 below that high and back inside the range, then 1789430400000 sells off to 2358.62 - a failed breakout / upthrust pattern and a 441-point round trip from the 2680 high.", "The last five bars (1789948800000-1790467199999) overlap inside 2633.31-2786.81 and none exceeds the 2850 high; the final close of 2694.96 is 155.04 below 2850, so the new-high breakout has no follow-through yet.", "1789948800000 closes 74.39 below its 2850 high and 1789776000000 leaves a 2786.81 upper wick, which is consistent with a buy-climax style push after three fast bull bars rather than a sustained channel."], "evidence_for": ["1787097600000 opens 1916.51 and closes 2252.16, clearing the 73-bar range top of 1974.46 by 277.70 on the close with only a 41.64 upper tail, followed by 1787270400000's 2771 high - a decisive bull breakout of the multi-month range rather than a single-bar probe.", "Swing lows after the spike rise or hold: 2111 (1787184000000), 2394.91 (1788134400000), 2357.18 (1788307200000) then 2358.62 (1789430400000) just 1.44 higher, and 2436.87 (1789689600000) - no lower low in the last 27 bars.", "1789689600000-1789948800000 closes 2612.02, 2632.98, 2642.9, 2775.61 hold above the 2357.18-2557.46 range, so the move above the post-spike range top has acceptance, not just wicks.", "The 2850 high of 1789948800000 exceeds the spike high of 2771 and the 2680 high of 1789084800000, keeping the swing sequence of higher highs and higher lows intact across the last 38 bars."], "missing_information": [], "observations": ["Window opens 1780099200000 at 2013.41 and falls to a 1368.42 low at 1780704000000, whose close of 1568.55 is 200.13 above its low (wide bear legs with a large final lower tail).", "1780790400000-1787011200000 (73 bars) overlap inside a 1512.91 (1782432000000 low) to 1974.46 (1785110400000 high) range; lows rise from 1512.91 to 1868.51 while highs stall at 1944.39-1974.46.", "The last 13 bars of that range (1786060800000-1787011200000) are small overlapping bars clustering in 1868.51-1937.76 directly before the expansion.", "Bar 1787097600000 opens 1916.51, closes 2252.16, with a 2293.8 high: a 388.17-range bull bar closing 277.70 above the prior 1974.46 range top.", "1787270400000 extends to 2771, then 1787356800000-1788998400000 (20 bars) overlap between 2357.18 (1788307200000 low) and 2557.46 (1787788800000 high).", "Bar 1789084800000 spikes to 2680 but closes 2514.72, 165.28 below that high and back inside the 20-bar range; 1789430400000 then puts in a 2358.62 low, 1.44 above the 2357.18 low.", "1789689600000-1789948800000 close 2612.02, 2632.98, 2642.9 and 2775.61, clearing the 2557.46 range top and the 2771 spike high; the 1789948800000 high is 2850, 74.39 above its close.", "1789948800000-1790467199999 (last five bars) overlap inside 2633.31-2786.81; the final bar opens 2690.56, closes 2694.96 at 2695.17 high and 2665.14 low, still 155.04 below the 2850 high."], "phase": "channel", "primary_regime": "bull-trend", "role": "CONTEXT_ANALYST", "schema": "brooks.market-context.v2", "structures": [{"description": "Sell climax / bear leg: five wide bear bars drive from 2030.49 down to 1368.42, ending with a large lower tail on 1780704000000 (close 1568.55).", "end_time_ms": 1780703999999, "kind": "climax", "lower_boundary": "1368.42", "start_time_ms": 1780099200000, "upper_boundary": "2030.49"}, {"description": "Large overlapping trading range after the sell-off: 1512.91-1974.46 over 73 bars, with gradually rising lows and capped highs; the final 13 bars tighten into 1868.51-1937.76 before expansion.", "end_time_ms": 1787011199999, "kind": "range", "lower_boundary": "1512.91", "start_time_ms": 1780790400000, "upper_boundary": "1974.46"}, {"description": "Bull spike out of the range: 1787097600000 opens 1916.51 and closes 2252.16 through 1974.46, 1787270400000 prints 2771, and 1787356800000 opens 2515.27 above the prior range top.", "end_time_ms": 1787356799999, "kind": "breakout", "lower_boundary": "1905.63", "start_time_ms": 1787097600000, "upper_boundary": "2771"}, {"description": "Twenty-bar post-spike overlap between 2357.18 and 2557.46; 1789084800000 pokes to 2680 but closes 2514.72 back inside this range.", "end_time_ms": 1788998399999, "kind": "range", "lower_boundary": "2357.18", "start_time_ms": 1787356800000, "upper_boundary": "2557.46"}, {"description": "Bull leg from the 2358.62 low of 1789430400000 to the 2850 high of 1789948800000; three consecutive bull closes (2612.02, 2632.98, 2642.9) carry above both the 2557.46 range top and the 2771 spike high.", "end_time_ms": 1789948799999, "kind": "swing", "lower_boundary": "2358.62", "start_time_ms": 1789430400000, "upper_boundary": "2850"}, {"description": "Five-bar overlap at the highs between 2633.31 and 2786.81 with no bar exceeding 2850; the final bar closes 2694.96 near its 2695.17 high.", "end_time_ms": 1790467199999, "kind": "two-sided", "lower_boundary": "2633.31", "start_time_ms": 1790035200000, "upper_boundary": "2786.81"}], "symbol": "ETH-USDT", "timeframe": "D1", "transition_conditions": ["Two consecutive closes above 2850 (1789948800000 high) with bars closing near their highs would confirm continuation of the 1789689600000-1789948800000 breakout and strengthen the bull-trend read.", "A close back below 2557.46 plus a break of 2436.87 (1789689600000 low) would end acceptance above the post-spike range top and return the read to a 2357-2850 trading range.", "Loss of the nearly equal lows at 2357.18 (1788307200000) and 2358.62 (1789430400000) would leave 2850 as a lower-high failure after 2771 and shift primary_regime toward trading-range or transition-unclear.", "Continued bar-by-bar overlap inside 2633.31-2786.81 without a new high keeps the current phase as a range at the highs rather than a resumed spike."], "window_bars": 120}, "freshness": "current"}, "H4": {"context": {"always_in": "long", "always_in_relevance": "low", "breakout_mode": true, "confidence": "medium", "decision_time_ms": 1790495999999, "directional_pressure": "bull", "evidence_against": ["Strongest counterargument: the window's dominant leg is the bull move 2358.62 (bar 51) to 2850.00 (bar 85), and the whole post-spike range has held above its 50% level near 2604, so this can equally be read as a bull flag / pullback inside an ongoing bull trend, with the tight final range as the flag.", "Bar 120 is a bull trend bar closing on its high after a higher low (2665.14 at bar 118) and it is the highest close in 24 bars; in Brooks terms that is the kind of bar that flips the short-term always-in long and can start a breakout from a tight range.", "The early window repeats the same sequence (bars 1-25 range, bar 26 spike, then another range before the next leg up), so a tight range here could be the same continuation process rather than a topping range.", "The stepping-down highs 2804.59 to 2786.81 to 2740.42 after the bar-85 spike with a large upper tail is also consistent with a possible final-flag / lower-high topping pattern, which would make the range a distribution area rather than a balanced one."], "evidence_for": ["The post-spike phase is genuinely two-sided: for bars 86-120 every close remains inside 2633.31-2772.99 and the 2700 area is tested repeatedly (bars 100-107 highs 2683.74-2699.53), the classic overlapping signature of a trading range rather than a channel.", "Structure is converging, not trending: highs step down 2804.59 (bar 88) to 2786.81 (bar 96) to 2740.42 (bar 109) while lows hold above 2633.31 (bar 103) and then 2665.14 (bar 118).", "The final 11 bars (109-119) shrink to roughly 9-27 point ranges, i.e. a tight range / breakout mode, which is a state of unresolved direction, not a directional trend.", "Bar 120's bull close at 2717.24 is only a minor probe: it is below the bar-110 high 2721.75 and 23.18 below the bar-109 high 2740.42, with no follow-through bar yet, so there is no acceptance above the range."], "missing_information": [], "observations": ["Bars 1-25 (open 1788768000000) oscillate in a 2411.04-2520.68 area near 2480; bar 26 spikes to 2680.00 (close 2555.52) but the advance stalls again between 2506.68 and 2609.02 through bar 45.", "Bars 46-51 sell off to the window low 2358.62 (bar 51 low, close 2412.95), then a strong bull leg runs from that low to the window high 2850.00 (bar 85 high) with strong bull closes at 2636.28 (bar 68) and 2723.15 (bar 85).", "Bar 85 is a wide 2658.81-2850.00 range bar closing 2723.15, leaving a 126.85 upper tail (spike/climax-type bar); price has not traded back above 2804.59 (bar 88 high) since.", "Bars 86-120 overlap heavily: every close sits between 2633.31 and 2772.99, the 2700 area is probed repeatedly (bars 100-107 highs 2683.74-2699.53), highs step down 2804.59 (bar 88) to 2786.81 (bar 96) to 2740.42 (bar 109) while lows hold above 2633.31 (bar 103 low; bar 118 low 2665.14).", "Bars 109-119 are a tight range: bar ranges of roughly 9-27 points, highs 2690.21-2740.42, lows 2665.14-2682.53, with no close giving back the bar-109 close of 2715.90.", "Bar 120 opens 2695.79, closes 2717.24 at its high (range 26.91), the highest close since bar 95 (2741.96), but its high 2717.27 remains below the bar-110 high 2721.75 and the bar-109 high 2740.42."], "phase": "range", "primary_regime": "trading-range", "role": "CONTEXT_ANALYST", "schema": "brooks.market-context.v2", "structures": [{"description": "Bull leg from the window low to the window high: strong bull bars (bar 68 close 2636.28; bar 85 close 2723.15) with only shallow overlapping pullbacks. The leg ends at the 2850.00 spike high that carried a large upper tail.", "end_time_ms": 1789991999999, "kind": "swing", "lower_boundary": "2358.62", "start_time_ms": 1789488000000, "upper_boundary": "2850"}, {"description": "Post-spike trading range: after the 2850.00 spike the market goes two-sided, with stepping-down highs 2804.59 / 2786.81 / 2740.42 and lows holding above 2633.31. Repeated probes of the 2700 area and overlapping closes are range behaviour, not an accepted break.", "end_time_ms": 1790495999999, "kind": "range", "lower_boundary": "2633.31", "start_time_ms": 1789992000000, "upper_boundary": "2804.59"}, {"description": "Tight final range / breakout mode: bars 109-119 contract to roughly 9-27 point ranges inside 2665.14-2740.42 with rising lows off 2665.14. Bar 120 probes the upper edge and closes at its high, but stays under the bar-109 high, so this is a two-sided breakout-mode area rather than a confirmed breakout.", "end_time_ms": 1790495999999, "kind": "breakout", "lower_boundary": "2665.14", "start_time_ms": 1790332800000, "upper_boundary": "2740.42"}], "symbol": "ETH-USDT", "timeframe": "H4", "transition_conditions": ["A close above 2740.42 (bar 109 high) followed by a second close above 2786.81 (bar 96 high) would move the read from range to a bull breakout-spike; failing to hold above 2740.42 keeps it as an in-range probe.", "A close below 2665.14 (bar 118 low) and then below 2633.31 (bar 103 low) with a bear follow-through bar would shift the read to a bear leg within the post-2850 drift.", "Continued closes between 2665.14 and 2740.42 with small overlapping ranges keeps the range / breakout-mode classification intact.", "A bull probe above 2740.42 that reverses with a bear bar closing near its low would reassert the stepping-down highs sequence and target the 2633.31 area of the range."], "window_bars": 120}, "freshness": "current"}}, "raw": {"H1": [{"close": "2749.09", "close_time_ms": 1790071199999, "high": "275